"""Plan item 3.6: what each state's own auditors found.
Default source: the state's latest single audit (the yearly audit of federal money every state must get), as filed with
the Federal Audit Clearinghouse. We show the largest questioned cost in it, or the auditor's own stated total when the
report gives one. Where the state auditor published a bigger finding in its own report, that is shown (AL, CA) or added
under "Also" (AZ). Each 'check' string must appear in the saved report text (data/states/auditors/raw/, not committed);
verify with: python3 -I state_audits.py
basis: known = questioned costs the auditors counted; likely = the auditors' projection from a sample;
       total = the report's own total for the year; report = a separate report by the state's auditor; none = no dollar amount."""

